1
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:41,000
What dies here...stays here.

2
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:16,000
The Drowned is a horror, drama, thriller film directed by Bruce G. Hallenbeck.

3
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Kate Williams inherits her grandmother's cottage on a remote lake.

4
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:26,000
There, she encounters apparitions that seem to emanate from a submerged church where a
congregation drowned over 100 years ago...but there is more than meets the eye.

5
00:22:55,000 --> 00:23:01,000
Kate Williams, played by Stephanie Tanaka.

6
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Edgar Van Dam, played by Nick Miscusi.

7
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Colleen O'Hanlon, played by Helen Black.

8
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Father Merrow, played by Jeff Kirkendall.

9
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Changeling, played by Vincent De Paul.

10
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:56,000
Jenny Greenteeth, played by Susan Hallenbeck.

11
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:31,000
Casino Royale is a 2006 spy thriller film, the twenty-first in the James Bond series by Eon Productions, the third screen adaptation of
Ian Fleming's 1953 novel of the same name, and the first to star Daniel Craig as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond.

12
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
The second entry in the film series to be directed by Martin Campbell, its screenplay was written by Neal Purvis,
Robert Wade, and Paul Haggis, and co-stars Eva Green, Mads Mikkelsen, Judi Dench, and Jeffrey Wright.

13
00:59:35,000 --> 00:59:41,000
In the film, Bond is on a mission to bankrupt the terrorism financier Le Chiffre
(Mikkelsen) in a high-stakes poker game at the Casino Royale in Montenegro.

14
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
Following Die Another Day (2002), Eon decided to reboot the franchise, attempting to provide a
realistic and darker exploration of a less experienced and more vulnerable Bond.

15
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
Casting involved a widespread search for a new actor to succeed Pierce Brosnan as Bond; the
choice of Craig, announced in October 2005, initially proved controversial.

16
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
Principal photography took place in the Bahamas, Italy, the United Kingdom, and the Czech Republic, with
interior sets built at Pinewood Studios and Barrandov Studios, from January to July 2006.

17
01:17:55,000 --> 01:18:01,000
The film features primarily practical stuntwork as opposed to the
computer-generated placements seen in other Bond films.

18
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
Casino Royale premiered at the Odeon Leicester Square on 14 November 2006, and was theatrically
released first in the United Kingdom on 16 November, and in the United States a day later.

19
01:27:05,000 --> 01:27:11,000
The film received critical acclaim, with praise for Craig's reinvention of the
character and the departure from the tropes of previous Bond films.

20
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:46,000
It grossed over $616 million worldwide, becoming the fourth highest-grossing film of 2006
and the highest-grossing James Bond film until the release of Skyfall (2012).

21
01:36:15,000 --> 01:36:21,000
A sequel, Quantum of Solace, was released in 2008.

22
01:40:50,000 --> 01:40:56,000
The film explores themes of insanity, water
monster, drowned, ghost, evil spirits.

23
01:45:25,000 --> 01:45:31,000
The tone is intense and dark and emotional.
